{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277798-share-your-villians","id":277798,"title":"Share your Villians","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-10T20:36:05-07:00","id":277798,"title":"Share your Villians","content":"im thinking on how meaninful &quot;The villians.&quot; in each game are. im struggling on a DtF campaing that slowly turning in a very VtM sort of Game (involving the houses and politics). I been thinking in using Metatron as a sort of Alien Being (Not outer space but demeanor) who gives a fuck about humanity, acts in a very steriotypical luciferian way (who can drive people insane or make their heads explote) and which main purpouse its only to foretold the message that &quot;Theres No God Anymore...&quot; and that demons are free to do what they wish. as a sign of the Armaggedon<br /> <br /> what villians have you made before?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T21:51:33-07:00","id":277874,"title":"","content":"One of my principle villains was Akna, the Balefire Phoenix. She was a fallen firebird spirit that devoted herself to Eater of Souls after she betrayed Falcon thousands of years ago. Her more recent machinations led to the corruption of a powerful Comanche warband who worshiped her as a twisted fertility goddess. Under her poisonous influence, a many among the Penateka Comanche, including women and children, began warping into self-mutilating monstrosities so blasphemous in appearance they could incited frenzy in nearly any Garou that looked at them. The Phoenix and her lair were finally destroyed during a joint attack by the Red Talons, Get of Fenris, and Bone Gnawers (with Uktena support behind the scenes). Warring with a being made of balefire resulted in many Garou warriors dying in the process, including a Red Talon elder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T16:36:56-07:00","id":286990,"title":"","content":"I have had a few in my time... but one of my favourites was the eternally scorned fallen silver fang Victor Bloodmoon. <br /> <br /> Victor was always beta to his older brother Roc... both Ahroun... and their sibling rivalry boiled over on many occassions. <br /> <br /> Victor's jealously of his brother culminated in a ham fisted attempt to shame Roc that ultimately resulted in a kinfolk's death and wyrm agents finding a caern of minor power. <br /> <br /> Roc exiled Victor but this mercy proved an error as Victor's banishment led to his insanity but also turn to the wyrm. For a number of years victor proved himself in battle with other spirals and acts of terror aganst gaian garou far away from Roc. Victor earned the favour of the eater-of-souls and ascended to a place of high renown amongst the dancers. But ever the megalomaniac, victor sought to further his power. This time over mortality itself.<br /> <br /> Now victor has returned to the lands of his brother... succesful in a horrid dark rite and now craves nightly the blood of mortals and of course... the shame of his brother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3371,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3371-digital-hiss","user":"Digital-hiss","date":". 10-19-2014, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3371-digital-hiss","name":"Digital-hiss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T04:00:53-07:00","id":287435,"title":"","content":"Most of the villains I've run weren't the &quot;big bad&quot; types. They have mostly been the PCs' peers, meeting them at cross-purposes due to differences in philosophy and/or conflicts of interest. Sometimes it's not always clear who the villains really are, and I've given my players plenty of chances to make friends or enemies out of a variety of NPCs. They've surprised me a few times by talking their way into a loose alliance of convenience when I expect a slash-and-burn approach, and by outright killing people who I thought they'd find useful.<br /> <br /> One of the few characters I used who was unabiguously a villain when I wrote him was Bishop Isadore Durant. He a Malkavian antitribu in power in Berkley, the city the PC's pack called home. He had maintained a secret alliance with the Camarilla for years. Each side fed the other empty &quot;victories&quot; and pre-arranged peace so the respective leaders could reinforce their power. He was known for a quirky and enigmatic personality which, combined with certain stereotype about his Clan, helped to avert scrutiny. Like many longer-lived vampires, Durant's only true loyality was to his own interests.<br /> <br /> As a flavor note, I think having a Malkavian constantly manipulating city politics to keep things convenient for the Sabbat gives tidy explanation of why Berkley, CA is such a ridiculous place. It certainly makes more sense than some of what actually goes on there sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":10,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","user":"Demon Cat","date":". 10-20-2014, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T08:07:39-07:00","id":287640,"title":"","content":"I've got a few go-to villains.<br /> <br /> Alexander Drake is my master planner/magnificent bastard. If he's a vampire, he's a Ventrue or a Setite. If he's a mage, he's NWO or Syndicate. He always wears a suit. He always has a plan. He does not get caught and if by some chance he does, not only is he not worried, but he has a plan for that too.<br /> <br /> Jake Malcolm is my boisterous brute. As a vampire, he's usually Gangrel or Brujah. If we're playing Changeling, he's a Redcap. He's big, loud, fights a lot, shoots first and might ask some questions later if he thinks about it.<br /> <br /> Zax Raven is my all-purpose con-man/trickster. As a vampire, he's Ravnos or Toreador (no, really, it works!). As a mage, he might be a barrabi VA or C of X, maybe not barrabi at all. He's trying to get something out of everybody and he doesn't care how he does it, as long as he doesn't have to work too hard for it and it won't seem like he worked to get it at all.<br /> <br /> The Professor (I change the last name around) is my generic mad scientist/creator. For Mage, I've made him an Etherite and a Progenitor. As a Wraith, he was an Artificer. He makes things, people, etc into whatever he thinks would be a better use of their materials or talents. He doesn't like the way the world is and so he's going to change it, one thing at a time if necessary, into the world he thinks it should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 10-21-2014, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T20:00:29-07:00","id":288175,"title":"","content":"I've got a Demon that my old players desperately want me to put up here... But it'll have to be tomorrow, as I am quickly dropping into unconsciousness. I'll leave you with this: what was supposed to be a simple fight turned into the Demon, for months afterwards, running through the Chinese Bells, tearing apart everything in his way, screaming &quot;VOOOOOORMAAAS!&quot; at the top of his lungs.<br /> <br /> It was all just a big misunderstanding, really. That's what makes it better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T07:20:17-07:00","id":288511,"title":"","content":"I have the Hag of Winter (aka the Stern Lady). It is a once-female 7th Generation Tzimisce embraced about 250 years ago. Heavily involved in the slave trade, her network of minions systematically bought, recovered or otherwise acquired unknown numbers of slaves (and others, later on) since then. These slaves were indoctrinated into various cults of her creation. Using the Apotheosis and Enfolding the Believers rituals, she has advanced in power to rival elders a millennium her senior. In addition to other Disciplines, her maxed-out Stamina, Fortitude and Serpentis 3 allow her to soak up almost any amount of damage and is a terrifying opponent.<br /> <br /> She appears in an area, using her Way of the Spirit koldunic powers to search for elders in torpor. She is unfailingly polite, versed in the French and southern etiquette of her living years. When she appears, she wants something, and it is best not to be in her path. She continues to be involved in human trafficking, with a Serpent minion helping her maintain and expand various cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","name":"g3taso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3814_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T08:03:50-07:00","id":288541,"title":"","content":"After writing this I realize all my recent villans have a distinctive mage-y touch to them. I will make sure to bend that trend!<br /> <br /> <br /> Three from my current game, far different &quot;story elements&quot; with each.<br /> <br /> First - The &quot;Far Beyond Redemption&quot; Villan<br /> <br /> Father Donovan, Barabbi Celestial Choir.<br /> He is a legendary Nephandi hunter, known to use brutal tactics and have no compassion for the twisted mage's souls. What most don't know is that he shares that same disregard for all souls. He believed (before the Cauls, because of the shit he saw) that we were all fundamentally tainted and union with God was only a pipe dream. Since the Cauls he takes pleasure in proving that even the most &quot;pious&quot; or well-meaning people have twisted souls. He works to caress this darkness out of them one small step at a time.<br /> He would rather die than admit what he truly is, and his conviction is hard to tell apart from a TV Evangelist.<br /> <br /> <br /> Second - The &quot;Good Intentions&quot; Villan<br /> <br /> Dr. Jonathan Jones, Progenitor<br /> He is a pharacopoeist who grew up on the streets before using his amazing intellect to work his way into an ivy league college. He spends his time now &quot;perfecting&quot; street drugs to remove all the &quot;unwanted&quot; side effects, and replace them with his own subtle social engineering-based side effects. Instead of meth making your teeth fall out, it makes you a better employee.<br /> <br /> <br /> Third - The &quot;Redeemable&quot; Villan<br /> <br /> (Name withheld for now)<br /> A hedge magician - alchemist with the OoH - who is beginning to get old and has lost hope of ever Awakening. He has lately turned to much darker research, and depending on how things go in the next few parts of the story could very easily fully fall into Infernalism. He isn't there yet, but he has made contact with a patron and done some minor thievery to further his own research, based on &quot;information&quot; provided by the demon.<br /> <br /> <br /> From a game long past, Dark Ages Vampire (with a splash of Mage and Werewolf).<br /> <br /> The Pot-Belly Merchant, Orphan Mind Mage, Infernalist (not Nephandi)<br /> His name changes frequently, and his only concern is making his life nice and comfortable. He was working with Lord Vanis because it was profitable, and he didn't give a shit how things turned out. His job - which he took very seriously - was to procure children and make sure they proceeded through the 'process' quickly.<br /> <br /> Lord Vanis, Tzimice 6th Generation, Infernalist, Rampant Diablerist<br /> An old world style ruler, and a master of fleshcrafting AND koldun. He was different in that he had a good deal of mage and spirit lore. He was able to blood bond a spirit mage, and incorporate this ability into his process. The process was simple, procure child -&gt; torture child -&gt; blood bond child -&gt; summon and force bane possession of child -&gt; Fleshcraft and train child to be elite (but prone to wild frenzies and the inability to feel good emotions) warrior.<br /> Lord Vanis would never fight directly and was deeply involved in Infernalism. He was exceptional at fleeing, and he could customize his minions to attack his enemies weaknesses. He didn't have many demonic investments, instead valuing knowledge and respect above all things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T18:58:21-07:00","id":291743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>g3taso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277798-share-your-villians?p=288511#post288511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the Hag of Winter (aka the Stern Lady). It is a once-female 7th Generation Tzimisce embraced about 250 years ago. Heavily involved in the slave trade, her network of minions systematically bought, recovered or otherwise acquired unknown numbers of slaves (and others, later on) since then. These slaves were indoctrinated into various cults of her creation. Using the Apotheosis and Enfolding the Believers rituals, she has advanced in power to rival elders a millennium her senior. In addition to other Disciplines, her maxed-out Stamina, Fortitude and Serpentis 3 allow her to soak up almost any amount of damage and is a terrifying opponent.<br /> <br /> She appears in an area, using her Way of the Spirit koldunic powers to search for elders in torpor. She is unfailingly polite, versed in the French and southern etiquette of her living years. When she appears, she wants something, and it is best not to be in her path. She continues to be involved in human trafficking, with a Serpent minion helping her maintain and expand various cults.</div> </div> </div> </div>Darn it, now I just had to go dig that character up, both versions in fact.<br /> <br /> The Hag of Winter / The Stern Lady VERSION 1.O<br /> Clan: Tzimisce (presumed)<br /> Nature: Idealist<br /> Demeanour: Perfectionist<br /> Generation: 7th<br /> Embrace: 1792<br /> Apparent Age: 35<br /> Physical: Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 6<br /> Social: Charisma 5, Manipulation 5, Appearance 4<br /> Mental: Perception 6, Intelligence 5, Wits 4<br /> Talents:<br /> Skills:<br /> Knowledges:<br /> Disciplines: Auspex 6, Celerity 2, Fortitude 6, Potence 3, Protean 2, Thaumaturgy 5, Vicissitude 4<br /> Thaumaturgical Paths: Way of the Spirit 3, Spirit Manipulation 4, Path of the Focused Mind 5<br /> Rituals: Enfolding the Believers, Rite of Apotheosis<br /> <br /> Madam Deveraux (The Stern Lady, The Hag of Winter) appears in cities across North America, particularly among the southern and port cities. She is immensely charismatic, possessed of a refined manner and exquisite decorum, dressed in beautiful but understated clothing which accentuates her beauty. Typically, she prefers etiquette and polite conversation when first engaged. When enraged, her <i>zulo</i> form combined with her Protean and physical powers make her a terrifying opponent. However, this is merely conjecture, as there are no existing survivor accounts. She is rumored to be associated with various blood cults past and present across the American South, and has extensive contacts in human trafficking.<br /> Background:<br /> Embraced from among the mulatto results of the African slave trade, the Kindred later known as The Stern Lady has been intimately connected with New Orleans and its history of slavery and spirit magics for centuries. Heir to a mortal magical tradition centered on the spirit world, she was brought into darkness by an unnamed vampire. Asserting control of several slaving ships with her emerging powers within a few years, she entered the slave trade as her own Mistress, embracing a variety of tutors to expand her knowledge. As her knowledge of blood and blood magic expanded, she found uses for the kine beyond merely serving as sustenance, binding them to her in chains of blood and secrecy for their vitae and other uses.<br /> The Stern Lady has the vision of becoming an antediluvian in her right, fueled by secret diablerie and the power of the kine souls she consumes in her pursuit of apotheosis. This steady stream of cultist souls has enabled her to grow in power to rival vampires greatly her senior. Through study she has realized that she is approaching the pinnacle of what her current generation is capable, and once more seeks an older cainite to diablerize to continue her ascension. Luckily she never shows the signs of diablerie!<br /> The Stern Lady is served by an elder Malkavian who possesses the <i>Restructure</i> power. This power is used in conjunction with Presence or Dominate to \u201crecruit\u201d individuals from homeless shelters or as a result of human trafficking into Soldier, Follower, Celebrant or other Natures for inclusion into their blood cults, creation of servants or agents, inclusion into special training or possibly childer.<br /> <br /> And here is the more advanced version<br /> The Hag of Winter / The Stern Lady VERSION 1.5<br /> Clan: Tzimisce (presumed)<br /> Nature: Idealist<br /> Demeanour: Perfectionist<br /> Generation: 5th<br /> Embrace: 1792<br /> Apparent Age: 35<br /> Physical: Strength 4, Dexterity 5, Stamina 7<br /> Social: Charisma 5, Manipulation 5, Appearance 4<br /> Mental: Perception 7, Intelligence 7, Wits 4<br /> Disciplines: Auspex 8, Celerity 2, Fortitude 7, Potence 5, Protean 2, Serpentis 3, Thaumaturgy 6, Vicissitude 8<br /> Thaumaturgical Paths: Way of the Spirit 3, Spirit Manipulation 4, Path of the Focused Mind 5<br /> Rituals: Enfolding the Believers, Rite of Apotheosis<br /> <br /> Note that in addition to improvements in Potence and Fortitude, Serpentis 3 allows this character to use the L6 Vicissitude power in conjunction with Serpentis 3 and Protean 2 in a single round.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","name":"g3taso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3814_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T19:43:16-07:00","id":291752,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">In my troupe\u2019s Wraith games, we had a few villains (in the \u201cBig Bad\u201d sense). We had one reoccurring character that was the troupe\u2019s primary antagonist without (necessarily) being the \u201cvillain.\u201d</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Sergeant Bigsley, Centurion of the Grim Legion and foil to our characters (of the lesser-evil variety). What we knew about him (or at least what the troupe put together) is that he\u2019s been dead for less than a century, is a protocol-driven military mind, and constant pain in the Corpus for the players. To him, we were:</span><br /> <ul><li>A borderline Heretic trucker probably in league with those shady Ferryman <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">(\u201cOnly the Ferryman could have forged that rig!\u201d)</span></span></li> <li>A reckless, vengeance-seeking outlaw on the verge of becoming Shadow-eaten. <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">(\u201cAnyone with that sorta grudge that crosses the Shroud that often has gotta be up to no good.\u201d)</span></span></li> <li>And a Doomed conspirator who is obviously a traitor to Stygia. <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">(\u201cWhy else would anyone associate with the riffraff that he\u2019s constantly seen with?\u201d</span></span>)</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">He\u2019s usually portrayed as a determined blend of Fidel Castro and Homer Simpson; a well-used field uniform (that we always thought was WWII-era), a pot-belly, a thick beard, and \u2013 yes! \u2013 a cigar. His legionnaires would harass us every chance they had, at one point arresting the troupe after a very unfortunate misunderstanding. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">As a plot device, I loved this character. He wasn\u2019t evil, he wasn\u2019t corrupt. He just took his job seriously. It just so happened, to our misfortune, that our characters\u2019 version of \u201cserious\u201d was not in-line with his. He was a great antagonist that a story could be created around that didn\u2019t end with some Big Nasty Nephwrack/Onceborn Cult/Pasiphae/etc.; we could save those for the stories that needed a touch of Oblivion-tainted Horror (capital &quot;H&quot;). </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Sgt. Bigsley, I salute you!</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T19:58:41-07:00","id":291759,"title":"","content":"I had a go to villain. She was a vampire called Olivia Deutreux. She was a Baali. She would be a perfect foil for everyone in all games since she had backup plans and contingencies for everything. Most of the minor dealings the players had with her was interfering with her plans to setup more backup plans. She was an evil Batman in that regard (pun intended).<br /> I had her have allies/frenemies in most every splat so that all of my players could deal with her because the people I played with loved her when they played VtM. Eventually, they ended up killing her. But I even made it one of those &quot;We saw her die. Right? Wait. Where's the body?&quot; sort of endings JUUUUUUST in case I wanted to use her again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T00:58:22-07:00","id":294608,"title":"","content":"One of my Mage characters was used as a villain in a friend's campaign. Don't know if it would be any good.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ram&quot;, a French Syndicate cosmetics magnate and fashion designer. Competed with that one Pentex subsidiary though his actions were just as bad. His whole focus was to sell &quot;Image&quot; (with a capital &quot;I&quot;). His work made teenage girls commit suicide because they weren't beautiful enough. He kept trying to redefine what the standards of beauty were. Sure, maybe there was still some animal testing going on in other countries.<br /> <br /> And maybe he had something to do with trying to remove the Delirium by convincing fangirls that werewolves are sexy... Never worked though. Paradox is an ugly bitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T06:27:23-07:00","id":294753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277798-share-your-villians?p=294608#post294608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my Mage characters was used as a villain in a friend's campaign. Don't know if it would be any good.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ram&quot;, a French Syndicate cosmetics magnate and fashion designer. Competed with that one Pentex subsidiary though his actions were just as bad. His whole focus was to sell &quot;Image&quot; (with a capital &quot;I&quot;). His work made teenage girls commit suicide because they weren't beautiful enough. He kept trying to redefine what the standards of beauty were. Sure, maybe there was still some animal testing going on in other countries.<br /> <br /> And maybe he had something to do with trying to remove the Delirium by convincing fangirls that werewolves are sexy... Never worked though. Paradox is an ugly bitch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I like this. I might steal this to combine with an idea I am working on, if you don't mind. I had gotten up too (in my head) 'encouraging abortions as a way to keep the free love alive', but I hadn't considered 'Image' so to speak.<br /> <br /> Refreshing take. +1 internets","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T06:57:28-07:00","id":294787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277798-share-your-villians?p=294753#post294753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I like this. I might steal this to combine with an idea I am working on, if you don't mind. I had gotten up too (in my head) 'encouraging abortions as a way to keep the free love alive', but I hadn't considered 'Image' so to speak.<br /> <br /> Refreshing take. +1 internets</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, thank you. I don't mind at all. It was a character from a long time ago. I've had a soft spot for the Syndicate with the whole &quot;money is faith, and we have a lot of faith&quot;, thing.<br /> <br /> Simply put, he was all about Mind and some Prime. Oh, and maybe a dot of Life. The only Rote I can remember was &quot;The art of self-consciousness&quot;, where he could insult someone's looks and stop them in their tracks. &quot;Seriously, I'm not going to talk to someone wearing that color tie with a blue blazer.&quot; But he was all about mass persuasion and using mental illusions to distract.<br /> <br /> My friend made him a villain for a Werewolf pack. My friend made him an egomaniac who harassed Werewolves because he could. At one point, his harassment became lethal, and he started having mercenaries hunt down Werewolves. He joked that Ram had become Cruella de Vil. He was actually hunting to force an Kinfolk employee of his to undergo the Skin Dancer ritual because he wanted to show he had the power to &quot;take Image to the next level&quot;. That became a core plot for his game.<br /> <br /> My friend passed away a few years ago, and I haven't played any WW games since then, so everything is, pardon the pun, fuzzy. I think &quot;Image&quot; was a malevolent Weaver spirit trying to set in stone what beauty was, and Ram was just an unknowing puppet. A puppet with his own cruel intentions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T07:34:17-07:00","id":294800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277798-share-your-villians?p=294787#post294787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, thank you. I don't mind at all. It was a character from a long time ago. I've had a soft spot for the Syndicate with the whole &quot;money is faith, and we have a lot of faith&quot;, thing.<br /> <br /> Simply put, he was all about Mind and some Prime. Oh, and maybe a dot of Life. The only Rote I can remember was &quot;The art of self-consciousness&quot;, where he could insult someone's looks and stop them in their tracks. &quot;Seriously, I'm not going to talk to someone wearing that color tie with a blue blazer.&quot; But he was all about mass persuasion and using mental illusions to distract.<br /> <br /> My friend made him a villain for a Werewolf pack. My friend made him an egomaniac who harassed Werewolves because he could. At one point, his harassment became lethal, and he started having mercenaries hunt down Werewolves. He joked that Ram had become Cruella de Vil. He was actually hunting to force an Kinfolk employee of his to undergo the Skin Dancer ritual because he wanted to show he had the power to &quot;take Image to the next level&quot;. That became a core plot for his game.<br /> <br /> My friend passed away a few years ago, and I haven't played any WW games since then, so everything is, pardon the pun, fuzzy. I think &quot;Image&quot; was a malevolent Weaver spirit trying to set in stone what beauty was, and Ram was just an unknowing puppet. A puppet with his own cruel intentions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sorry about your friend, and that all makes great sense!<br /> <br /> I think I will borrow some traits, but my eventual goal is a 'Cult of Personality' type thing that -seems- like a group the Cult and the Verbena could get behind, but ends up carrying their ideas to extremes that violate fundamentals - such as pressuring others into trying/doing stuff, abortions, clique-like behavior that goes from mean to violent.<br /> <br /> What I like is the angle on Image. I was looking for something that could be offensive without being... offensive, if that makes any sense? Image was something I hadn't messed with so I'm happy to pilfer and keep working on this new villain of mine. <br /> <br /> Thanks. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T12:21:20-07:00","id":295066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277798-share-your-villians?p=294800#post294800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry about your friend, and that all makes great sense!<br /> <br /> I think I will borrow some traits, but my eventual goal is a 'Cult of Personality' type thing that -seems- like a group the Cult and the Verbena could get behind, but ends up carrying their ideas to extremes that violate fundamentals - such as pressuring others into trying/doing stuff, abortions, clique-like behavior that goes from mean to violent.<br /> <br /> What I like is the angle on Image. I was looking for something that could be offensive without being... offensive, if that makes any sense? Image was something I hadn't messed with so I'm happy to pilfer and keep working on this new villain of mine.<br /> <br /> Thanks. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to see what you come up with. Hell, I may pilfer what you've pilfered and modified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T09:31:38-07:00","id":298250,"title":"","content":"Alexander is a man with simple beliefs, he wants to make a better world by destroying this one. His goal is to create a threat so monstrous to humanity, that they must unite to defend it or die trying. His goal is to make an army of monsters that are like the monsters of humanity's nightmares, and then unleash them upon the world. Sending them out to pillage and destroy, forcing a nuclear inferno to wipe the world clean. It would be after this that the men of this new world will rise up and grow stronger, united together to never let the world fall again into that terrible world of darkness it once was.<br /> <br /> His motives are arguably more correct than the PC's as they wish to hide in the shadow of the masquerade and control the world while he's about shaping it into a better place but has to paint over the canvas as it is to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T20:44:20-07:00","id":298655,"title":"","content":"Probably my most epic/fun villain was &quot;Ms. Romanov&quot;, a tzimisce elder who predated the Camarilla and Sabbat, and would often remind those around her that she was older than their &quot;mystery cults and secret societies&quot; (which she said so often, it became a trademark).<br /> <br /> Originally a Dark Ages character I played, &quot;Ms. Romanov&quot; eventually got 'ported over to my VtM game per the request of another player from that game. I didn't know where to possibly fit her in with a straight Cam game that wouldn't have any Sabbat appearances for a long time in my grand scheme until I looked at my scheming Nosferatu whose backstory hadn't been revealed (or, y'know, written). So with a minor mental retcon, I decided this Nos was &quot;Ms. Romanov&quot; in disguise, trying to lay low until she could cause total chaos among the Cammies, have them at each others' throats, make them weak, then take the city for herself (the same scheme the Nos was working on, but instead of becoming prince, &quot;Ms. Romanov&quot; planned to go all batship insane and remake it into some feudal territory). Through rumor spreading, false leads, and impersonating key figures doing un-good things, she manages to cause such a calamity among the locals, that her plan nearly succeeded. The best part (for me) was when the players finally realized it was the &quot;nosferatu&quot; behind everything all along. I dropped all kinds of clues and red herrings, but what finally caused them to look closer at the nos was a single conversation they had, where they realized the only person they all didn't want to kill was said nosferatu. &quot;When almost everyone around you is acting sketchy, the clear sketchiest motherfluxer is the one never acting sketchy&quot; was the summary of their thought process. They confronted the nos with guns, knives and claws ready and crapped their pants when the nosferatu when all zulo form and summoned &quot;it's&quot; vicissitude-enhanced minions. The fight ended with &quot;Ms. Romanov&quot; fleeing through the sewers.<br /> <br /> Months later (years in game), now with the characters in high ranking positions within the city, a &quot;foreign Tremere&quot; arrived and quickly made herself an ally of the coterie. More shenanigans ensued and as part of the city was burning, they thought they had their enemy cornered and &quot;unmasked&quot; the Tremere. Fighting stuff happens, the &quot;Tremere&quot; dies, and as the body turns to ask, the Vicissitude alterations melt away and reveal...<br /> <br /> A caitiff they had assumed fled the region.<br /> <br /> For years, they have played this cat-and-mouse game with &quot;Ms. Romanov&quot;, thinking they have her cornered, only to reveal it's someone altered in her shape, or she flees, or she was never the villain to begin with. Recently they became less interested in feuding with her and more interested in learning who she is (they only recently got the probable name of &quot;Ms. Romanov&quot; and until then, they called her &quot;The Tzimisce&quot;), why she even wants this city, and what other plots she's had in motion elsewhere in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T01:01:40-08:00","id":301931,"title":"","content":"About 100 years ago malcolm was a bare knuckle boxer in Australia. Tall mean and violent he quickly caught the eye of a brujah elder. Prohibited from embracing malcolm at this point in time the elder ghouled him and there malcolm stayed ever at his master's side. Protecting him through the day and running his errands.<br /> <br /> 100 years later and malcolm is his head of security and the brujah is prince. Malcolm's skills of daytime thuggery and his network of day contacts are far too valuable for the embrace... but Malcolm still holds an elevated position in the local court and with it much gravitas in the kindred community.<br /> <br /> Recently however Malcolm's heavy handed treatment of a young police investigator have caused a bit of a problem. The investigator has taken upon himself to get the bottom of the mystery that is malcolm and of course a 100 year old poster for bare knuckle brawling he was handed by a stranger that bears malcolm's likeness.<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> Malcolm of course was the main villain in my hunter game that run for a good year... eventually they killed him... but he was a far more difficult opponent than his stat sheet or place in oWod would normally dictate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3371-digital-hiss","name":"Digital-hiss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}